From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:15:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 43/43] core: a keystroke draws only what it changed

Every key that writes to the pty drew a frame twice over: the surface
queued a render to show the selection it clears and the viewport it
scrolls to the bottom, and the IO thread redrew after draining the
write from its mailbox. Most keys change nothing on screen: the
selection is empty, the viewport is at the bottom, and a write shows
nothing until the program answers. That frame still goes to the app,
and on GTK it can take the refresh: the frame with the program's echo,
ready a millisecond later, waits for the compositor's frame callback
of the one before. A key now queues a render only when it cleared a
selection or moved the viewport, and a write in the mailbox doesn't
redraw. The echo's output queues its own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Surface.zig       | 14 ++++++++++++--
 src/termio/Thread.zig |  9 +++++++--
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Surface.zig b/src/Surface.zig
index 3025103f5..31b68a50f 100644
--- a/src/Surface.zig
+++ b/src/Surface.zig
@@ -3028,15 +3028,25 @@ pub fn keyCallback(
         hotty.lockState(self, @src()); // hottyterm: the wait, stamped
         defer self.renderer_state.mutex.unlock(global.io());
 
+        // Draw only what the key changed. Until the program answers, a key
+        // that clears no selection and moves no viewport has nothing to
+        // show, and a frame drawn now could take the refresh that the
+        // answer's frame needs.
+        const screen = self.io.terminal.screens.active;
+        var changed = false;
         if (self.config.selection_clear_on_typing or
             event.key == .escape)
         {
+            changed = screen.selection != null;
             try self.setSelection(null);
         }
 
-        if (self.config.scroll_to_bottom.keystroke) self.io.terminal.scrollViewport(.bottom);
+        if (self.config.scroll_to_bottom.keystroke) {
+            changed = changed or !screen.viewportIsBottom();
+            self.io.terminal.scrollViewport(.bottom);
+        }
 
-        try self.queueRender();
+        if (changed) try self.queueRender();
     }
 
     return .consumed;
diff --git a/src/termio/Thread.zig b/src/termio/Thread.zig
index 79cdf8936..5caaaa1bb 100644
--- a/src/termio/Thread.zig
+++ b/src/termio/Thread.zig
@@ -306,8 +306,13 @@ fn drainMailbox(
     // ENOUGH to not mess up throughput on producers.
     var redraw: bool = false;
     while (mailbox.pop(global.io())) |message| {
-        // If we have a message we always redraw
-        redraw = true;
+        // If we have a message we always redraw, except for a write: what
+        // goes to the pty shows nothing until the program answers, and
+        // its output wakes the renderer itself.
+        redraw = redraw or switch (message) {
+            .write_small, .write_stable, .write_alloc => false,
+            else => true,
+        };
 
         log.debug("mailbox message={s}", .{@tagName(message)});
         switch (message) {
